{"content":[{"c":["DIVES*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Traditional name of the rich man in Christ’s parable about the beggar Lazarus (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.16.19-31","r":"Luke.16.19-31","rawR":"Luke.16.19-31","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.16.19-31","value":"Luke.16.19-31"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 16:19-31"},"). It came from the Latin term ",{"c":["dives,"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," translating a Greek word for “rich,” “wealthy.” Though the rich man was not named in the parable, this name was already well accepted in the church by the third century. A second-century Egyptian scribe gave him the name “Neves,” meaning “nothing.” ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Lazarus_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Lazarus_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Lazarus_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Lazarus #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Dives","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Lk 16:19-31","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.16.19-31","rawQueryValue":"Luke.16.19-31","sourceRefExact":"Luke.16.19-31"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"41d588805786257183ec96a4d0062a0945c88b031a413e63accb54ece117a6b5","sourceItemName":"Dives","sourceItemOrder":134,"sourceMember":"Articles/D.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Dives","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Dives*","title":"Dives*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}